id: command
name: Command
type: instant
actionCost: 0
kiCost: 0
attacking: false
requiresTarget: false
source: Core Rule
description: >
  Control your Minions: as many as your Standard Actions, each one an Action of yours,
  gain their Act Phase and a Counter Action.
text: >
  Command: Control your Minions!
  –Maneuver Type: Instant
  –Action Cost: N/A
  –KP Cost: N/A
  –Exploitable: N/A
  –Effect: Target a number of your Minions up to the number of Standard Actions you
  possess. You lose those Actions, but those Minions gain access to their Act Phase
  (see: Follower, Minions) and 1 Counter Action.

---

# Your Minions: your Settings tab's Minions list, and every Minion naming you its Master (allies.mjs minionsOf). Picked up to
# the Standard Actions left; those Actions lost, and each picked Minion has its Act Phase this Combat Round - its Attacking
# Maneuvers open, its turn not skipped (Follower) - and a Counter Action more (chat.mjs commandMinions).
[on used]
commandMinions();
